# Rust
/src-tauri/target/
# Cargo.lock IS committed — Relay ships as an application, not a library:
# a pinned lockfile gives reproducible builds across dev machines and CI.

# Node
node_modules/
dist/

# Local data — never commit real service/sermon data
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# STT models — large binaries, downloaded per-machine (see README dev setup)
/models/
*.bin

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.local

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/

# Local agent-tooling state (claude-flow / ruflo). Per-machine scratch — memory
# databases, metrics, backups. Kept out so `git status` still shows only real
# changes; nothing here is part of Relay.
/.claude-flow/
/.swarm/
/.agents/
/.claude/*

# …except Relay's OWN agent tooling, which is part of the project and travels with
# the clone: the QA audit agents encode this product's safety rules, and a
# contributor who does not get them will write a report that lies politely.
# Negations need the parent listed, hence `/.claude/*` above rather than `/.claude/`.
!/.claude/agents/
/.claude/agents/*
!/.claude/agents/relay-qa-*.md
!/.claude/commands/
/.claude/commands/*
!/.claude/commands/qa-audit.md
!/.claude/hooks/

# settings.json stays out on purpose — it is a MACHINE configuration, not Relay's,
# and committing it would hand every contributor whatever wiring one developer happened
# to have. Its contents differ per machine by definition, which is why this comment no
# longer describes them: an earlier version said "12 hook points, a status line, daemon
# schedules", and the file in this checkout holds exactly ONE entry — Relay's own fast
# gate. Check yours with `python3 -m json.tool .claude/settings.json`.
#
# A hook can only be declared in a settings file, so registration is per machine and
# one command:
#     npm run hooks:install     # idempotent; adds one entry, touches nothing else
#     npm run hooks:check       # exits 1 if it is not registered

# Generated by the release workflow: per-build Windows code-signing config
# (certificate thumbprint / signCommand). Never committed.
/src-tauri/tauri.winsign.conf.json
backgrounds-originals/

# Design-tool caches (local only)
.impeccable/
